Z||000013||skitime||08-22-2001||11:24 PM||||Hey Justin,<P>Come to the PA BBQ this Saturday.  You could bring your dad and talk Fieros all day.||||reg||1
Z||000014||BlackARROW||08-23-2001||01:49 AM||||Godsend, is it like working in a Supra 3.0l Turbo?  I know there is space, but the whole motor, turbo, AC, battery, etc, just take the whole space.  You just think of relocating stuff when you think of modifying "big time"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  What a car anyway.. Woooo!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Galen||08-23-2001||02:32 AM||||Ed, you talk too much junk  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>my first car was/is a 88 Coupe.. I bought it for 200$ with a blown engine. Threw a rod at like 120k miles. I got a 87 for 200$ and replaced the engine(me & my dad did) without a problem. I have no had any major problems out of it, other than a problem that is my fault. I need to replace a pulley that is causing belts to go bad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> but anyways.. All I've replaced is a oxygen sensor, dogbone(free <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), motor mount and changed the tranny filter. I've had misc other little problems that all pertain to my own ignorance(loose clamps and the such) or other ppls stupidity(1 1/2 foot crack from a Full sized 4x4 chevy truck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)...<P>Would I recommend a Fiero as a first car for someone, surely. I find them no harder to work on than any other car, you just have to keep a open mind about things and not let peoples opinions rule you. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000016||coolcat||08-23-2001||05:37 AM||||I too purchased a Fiero as my first car. I bought my first 87GT(RIP)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> when I was 17. I'm now 19 and own yet another 87GT. My first one was great no major mechanical problems at all, the only thing that had to be replaced  except for routine things was the cat. Don't let other people discourage you from getting one. If that's what you want go for it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Fiero's are Beautiful machines and  their owners are some of the nicest and most helpful out there.<P>But (theres always a "but") since you are 16 the insurance is gonna hit you like a tone of bricks. I have a clean record and I still pay about 250 a month . <P>hope you get it keep us posted.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headbang.gif"> Gettin good players is easy,gettin them to play together is the hard part||||reg||1
